WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/data-display/SourceLayerBadge.tsx — a PURE presentational atom (a debugger-only
  badge showing which live-state layer a signal value came from). Its ONLY hook is useTranslation; there is
  NO data query (the prompt itself records "Data sources: useTranslation" and "Charts/maps used: none").
    key   = (source ?? 'unknown').toLowerCase(); style = STYLE[key] ?? STYLE.unknown
    STYLE : l1 (emerald "L1") · l2 (blue "L2") · log (neutral "LOG") · stale (amber "STALE") · unknown ("—")
    formatAge(ms): null/!finite => null · <1000 => "{round(ms)} ms" · <60_000 => "{(ms/1e3)→1dp} s"
                   · <3_600_000 => "{round(ms/6e4)} min" · <86_400_000 => "{(ms/3.6e6)→1dp} h" · else "{(ms/8.64e7)→1dp} d"
    tooltip = ageText ? `${t(descKey,descFallback)} (${t('sourceLayer.age','age')}: ${ageText})` : t(descKey,descFallback)
    <Tooltip content={tooltip}><span data-source={key} className=… min-w 1.5rem|2.5rem>{style.label}</span></Tooltip>
  Quirk reproduced verbatim (NOT "fixed"): showLabel only WIDENS the badge (min-w 2.5rem vs 1.5rem); it does
  NOT change the glyph text — the rendered label is always style.label (the web doc-comment claims otherwise;
  the CODE is the contract, per the predecessor "do NOT fix the arithmetic" discipline).

