  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO shared-surfaces errors; ALL blockers pre-exist this change, VERIFIED
  on THIS worktree, not assumed):
    1. Duplicate types in the app module — `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` is DEFINED 15× across
       Sources/DashboardWidgets/* + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/* (and `PowerFlowConnection` 2×). Swift forbids this:
       a 2-file reproduction `swiftc -typecheck` of two `public struct DashboardWidgetSize {}` files prints
       "error: invalid redeclaration of 'DashboardWidgetSize'" (exit 1) — so the app target CANNOT compile,
       a language guarantee independent of this surface, the framework, or the runner.
    2. 224 co-located *.Tests.swift under feature-views/ + dashboard-widgets/ import XCTest into the APP target.
       This surface's test is the ONLY co-located test correctly EXCLUDED from the app target (project.yml excludes,
       verified via xcodegen membership above), so it adds ZERO to that pre-existing pile.
    3. Frameworks/Shared.xcframework is not staged on this worktree (the scheme pre-action runs a long Kotlin/Native
       Gradle assemble; ADR-004). macOS additionally requires a development SIGNING certificate (ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME).
    A faithful `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync … build test` WAS launched on this runner; it advanced through the
    Gradle Shared.xcframework pre-action under heavy parallel-slot contention (Gradle reported 15 busy daemons),
    and the shared /tmp capture file was reaped by a concurrent slot before completion, so a final exit code is not
    pasted here — but the failure is conclusively PRE-EXISTING per (1)–(3) and matches the predecessor
    p4-apple/feature-views/0010-ToolCard log (same Xcode 26.5 runner: IOS_EXIT=65 / MAC_EXIT=65 on the SAME
    DashboardWidgetSize collisions + signing). These are owned by the P4/P99 Apple acceptance gate on a signed
    macos-latest CI runner per apps/macos-pending-verifications.md (row added) — NOT by a single shared-surface prompt
    (task rule: do not fix pre-existing unrelated breakage). The xcodegen-generated .xcodeproj is git-ignored.

